# Testing

## Test Suite

All testing is done via **integration tests** in the `test/` directory using Python pytest.

## Building

**Do NOT use `make`** — that builds the original C codebase. Instead:

```bash
# Build the Rust port
cargo build

# Copy binary to repo root (required for tests)
cp target/debug/pgbouncer .
```

## Test Environment Setup

```bash
# Create and activate Python virtual environment
python3 -m venv env
source env/bin/activate
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Ensure PostgreSQL server binaries are in PATH
# On macOS with Homebrew:
export PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/postgresql@18/bin:$PATH"
# Adjust version number as needed (e.g., postgresql@17)

# Required for PostgreSQL 18+ on macOS:
export LC_ALL=C
```

## Running Tests

```bash
# Activate environment first
source env/bin/activate
export PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/postgresql@18/bin:$PATH"
export LC_ALL=C

# Run all tests
cd test && pytest

# Run specific test file
pytest test_admin.py

# Run specific test
pytest test_admin.py::test_show

# Run with verbose output
pytest test_admin.py -v

# Run with timeout (recommended)
pytest test_admin.py --timeout=120
```

## Quick Test Command (from repo root)

```bash
cargo build && cp target/debug/pgbouncer . && \
  source env/bin/activate && \
  export PATH="/opt/homebrew/opt/postgresql@18/bin:$PATH" && \
  export LC_ALL=C && \
  cd test && pytest test_admin.py -v
```

